  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * Complex Matrix multiplication is only defined if the number of columns of the
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * first matrix equals the number of rows of the second matrix.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * Multiplying an <code>M x N</code> matrix with an <code>N x P</code> matrix results
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * in an <code>M x P</code> matrix.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * When matrix size checking is enabled, the functions check: (1) that the inner dimensions of
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrcA</code> and <code>pSrcB</code> are equal; and (2) that the size of the output
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  * matrix equals the outer dimensions of <code>pSrcA</code> and <code>pSrcB</code>.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c ****  */
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_cmplx_mult_f32.c **** 
